WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.082
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:09.478
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.778 --> 00:00:16.377
Unit ten: Angkor Wat. In this unit, you will talk about Cambodia's most famous temple.

4
00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:18.535
Angkor Wat.

5
00:00:19.235 --> 00:00:23.290
Angkor Wat means the largest temple in the world, in Cambodia.

6
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.473
Angkor Wat is on our flag.

7
00:00:26.173 --> 00:00:29.162
Your turn. Say: Angkor Wat.

8
00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:32.852
Angkor Wat.

9
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.700
Temple.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.957
Temple means a building where people pray.

11
00:00:38.257 --> 00:00:40.036
There are many temples in Siem Reap.

12
00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:43.377
Your turn. Say: Temple.

13
00:00:46.077 --> 00:00:46.857
Temple.

14
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:48.677
Stone.

15
00:00:49.377 --> 00:00:52.305
Stone means a hard material from the ground.

16
00:00:52.605 --> 00:00:54.814
The temple is made of stone.

17
00:00:55.514 --> 00:00:58.282
Your turn. Say: Stone.

18
00:01:00.982 --> 00:01:01.879
Stone.

19
00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:03.617
King.

20
00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:06.700
King means a man who rules a country.

21
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.000
A Khmer king built Angkor Wat.

22
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.957
Your turn. Say: King.

23
00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:15.426
King.

24
00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:17.255
Old.

25
00:01:17.955 --> 00:01:20.152
Old means made a long time ago.

26
00:01:20.452 --> 00:01:22.278
The temple is very old.

27
00:01:22.978 --> 00:01:25.177
Your turn. Say: Old.

28
00:01:27.877 --> 00:01:28.750
Old.

29
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:30.763
Visitors.

30
00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:34.147
Visitors means people who come to see a place.

31
00:01:34.447 --> 00:01:36.389
Many visitors come every day.

32
00:01:37.089 --> 00:01:40.310
Your turn. Say: Visitors.

33
00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:43.825
Visitors.

34
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:45.911
Sunrise.

35
00:01:46.611 --> 00:01:49.516
Sunrise means the time when the sun comes up.

36
00:01:49.816 --> 00:01:51.479
We watched the sunrise.

37
00:01:52.179 --> 00:01:55.353
Your turn. Say: Sunrise.

38
00:01:58.053 --> 00:01:59.008
Sunrise.

39
00:02:00.017 --> 00:02:00.960
Siem Reap.

40
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.414
Siem Reap means the city near Angkor Wat.

41
00:02:04.714 --> 00:02:06.621
We took a bus to Siem Reap.

42
00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:09.764
Your turn. Say: Siem Reap.

43
00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:13.372
Siem Reap.

44
00:02:14.383 --> 00:02:16.650
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.414
Rithy, have you been to Angkor Wat?

46
00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:23.601
Yes! I went with my family last year.

47
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:26.022
Who built it?

48
00:02:27.317 --> 00:02:31.278
It was built by a Khmer king, King Suryavarman the Second.

49
00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:33.956
What did you do there?

50
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.158
We watched the sunrise. It was beautiful!

51
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.705
Grammar focus: It was built .

52
00:02:42.005 --> 00:02:44.457
Angkor Wat was built by a Khmer king.

53
00:02:44.757 --> 00:02:48.405
Use 'was built' when the building is more important than the builder.

54
00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:52.545
Now read and listen. The Pride of Cambodia.

55
00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:55.948
Angkor Wat is a huge stone temple near Siem Reap.

56
00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.875
It was built by a Khmer king more than 800 years ago.

57
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:04.647
It is the largest temple in the world.

58
00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.517
Many visitors come to watch the sunrise behind its towers.

59
00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:15.034
Angkor Wat is on the Cambodian flag, and we are very proud of it.

60
00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.654
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:18.954 --> 00:03:21.604
Angkor Wat was blank by a Khmer king.

62
00:03:21.904 --> 00:03:24.919
A, build. B, built. C, building.

63
00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.405
The answer is B: built.

64
00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:33.626
Angkor Wat is near blank.

65
00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:37.788
A, Siem Reap. B, Kampot. C, Battambang.

66
00:03:41.783 --> 00:03:44.166
The answer is A: Siem Reap.

67
00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.893
The time when the sun comes up is blank.

68
00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:52.276
A, sunset. B, sunrise. C, night.

69
00:03:56.283 --> 00:03:58.782
The answer is B: sunrise.

70
00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:03.644
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you know about Angkor Wat?

71
00:04:08.944 --> 00:04:14.475
Angkor Wat was built by a Khmer king. It is made of stone, and it is on our flag.

72
00:04:14.775 --> 00:04:16.520
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:17.517 --> 00:04:21.597
Great work today! You learned eight new words and it was built .

74
00:04:21.897 --> 00:04:26.802
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

75
00:04:27.102 --> 00:04:29.963
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

76
00:04:30.263 --> 00:04:33.310
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

